# The local nodes' own Tor client (tor-socks in compose.nodes-tor.yaml, A-442): one SOCKS port for bitcoind and monerod,
# nothing else. It is not the onion service's deploy/torrc: that container keeps SocksPort 0 and this one runs no onion
# service. docs/operator-guide.md#local-nodes-over-tor says what goes through it and what does not.
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
Log notice stdout
# Well inside the container's 256m mem_limit (see deploy/torrc).
MaxMemInQueues 128 MB
ControlPort 0
# Only tor-socks's own address on the node network (node_egress, internal; compose.nodes-tor.yaml pins the subnet
# 10.199.42.0/28 and this address), so its egress network reaches no SOCKS port. Change both files together.
# Keep node/client addresses, supplied SOCKS credentials and peer destination addresses/ports on separate
# circuits. This is stream isolation within this Tor process, not a guarantee against traffic correlation.
SocksPort 10.199.42.2:9050 IsolateSOCKSAuth IsolateClientAddr IsolateDestAddr IsolateDestPort
# Only the nodes: the node network, except its gateway (the host's bridge address); everything else is refused.
SocksPolicy reject 10.199.42.1
SocksPolicy accept 10.199.42.0/28
SocksPolicy reject *
